<Placemark>   <name>Grindheim stone cross</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Cross <b>County/Region:</b> Hordaland <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 59.669598 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 6.003846<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Scandinavia/Norway/thumb/DSCF0697mc4_393.JPG" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Ancient Cross in Hordaland<br />This ancient stone cross was found in the garden of a nearby farm. It was dug up and placed just outside the church building around 10 metres away from the church wall ...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=32547" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>6.003846,59.669598,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Krosshaug Barrow</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Cross <b>County/Region:</b> Rogaland <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 58.753794 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 5.636458<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Scandinavia/Norway/thumb/DSCF1402mc3_1145.JPG" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Ancient Cross in Rogaland<br />Krosshaug consists of an old stone cross placed on top of an older iron age round barrow. The cross has probably been made in the earliest period of Christianity in Norw...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=32364" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#46_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>5.636458,58.753794,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark></Folder><Folder><name><![CDATA[Ancient Palace]]></name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>   <name>Kongsgaarden</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Palace <b>County/Region:</b> Oslo <b>Alt Name:</b> Oslo kongsgård <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>3</b>  Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 59.903528 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 10.76321<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Scandinavia/Norway/thumb/kongsgaarden_-_IMG_8005.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Kongsgaarden was the fortified residence of King Harald Hardrada (1015-1066). The founding of the residence is widely recognized as the beginning of today`s Norwegian capital Oslo. The death of Hardra...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=53402" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#61_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>10.76321,59.903528,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark></Folder><Folder><name><![CDATA[Ancient Village or Settlement]]></name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>   <name>Anda-Grønhaug</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>County/Region:</b> Rogaland <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>3</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>3</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 58.771073 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 5.654088<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Scandinavia/Norway/thumb/20200720_105644.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Ancient Village or Settlement in Rogaland. Grønhaug is a large round barrow located in a large flat grazing ground for cows. I was only able to get some good photos from outside the stone fence surro...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=54272" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>5.654088,58.771073,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Åse settlement</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>Alt Name:</b> Åse tunanlegg <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>5</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>5</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 69.008119 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 15.755939<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Scandinavia/Norway/thumb/Ase2.JPG" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    This site is a ancient settlement from the Iron age, and is basically the same as the one on Vollmoen in Steigen. It consists of 14 structures, probably houses in two crescent-shaped rows forming a ci...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
